  grep -rl --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=dist "@license Enterprise" packages

  4. What this means for your rebrand

  1. Don't ship Enterprise features in production unless you buy a subscription. That means no SSO, row-level permissions, audit logs, usage analytics, custom domains or Twenty's billing. If you need
     them, write your own versions from scratch without copying the Enterprise code.
  2. Removing the Twenty name is fine, since AGPL allows rebranding. I found no trademark policy in the repo, but AGPL §7(e) lets Twenty refuse use of its trademarks. So removing "Twenty" names and
     logos is the safe choice, which is what your feat-rebrand branch is doing.
  3. Leave license and copyright notices alone. Don't remove LICENSE or the "Copyright Twenty.com, PBC" lines while rebranding.
  4. Publish your source. If this CRM will be offered to users over a network, publish the source of your fork (for example, a public repo linked from the app).

  If you want, I can write a script that flags Enterprise files your rebrand touches, or map the Enterprise modules the rest of the code depends on so they can be switched off cleanly.
